Android's byte order for Skia's 32-bit pixels (ADR-0043 test 2).

The host flavor takes Skia's linux config, whose SK_R32_SHIFT 16 makes kN32 BGRA, as layoutlib wants for Java's int
ARGB images. Android's framework build leaves it to Skia's default, RGBA everywhere but Windows (SkTypes.h), which
Bitmap.Config.ARGB_8888 documents for copyPixelsToBuffer: R, G, B, A in memory. With BGRA, every raw pixel an app
reads or writes, and every buffer handed on unconverted, had red and blue swapped. So the define goes, and kN32 is
RGBA, as on a device.

--- a/external/skia/linux/include/config/SkUserConfig.h
+++ b/external/skia/linux/include/config/SkUserConfig.h
@@ -67,10 +67,6 @@
 #define SK_HAS_WUFFS_LIBRARY
 #endif
 
-#ifndef SK_R32_SHIFT
-#define SK_R32_SHIFT 16
-#endif
-
 #ifndef SK_SUPPORT_PDF
 #define SK_SUPPORT_PDF
 #endif
